Same program (the Calculator::Ast port's generator and parser, run once in prepare as the reference does) and the same evaluator: a recursive walk over the tree, numbers, variable reads (0 when unset), the five operators with wrapping +, - and * (the wrapping_add, wrapping_sub and wrapping_mul builtins, added for this port) and the reference's simple_div and simple_mod, assignments storing their value; a new variable map every run; the result is the last expression's value. As in the Calculator::Ast port the reference's Box nodes are arrays filled by a bump counter (prepare is untimed; the run only reads the tree). The reference's HashMap<String, i64> is lib/strmap.mito; a variable's name is cut out of the program text with text_from, which copies it into the request's text area (the reference borrows the node's String); that area is given back after each expression. Stores are checked and undo-logged.
